    "note_tweet": {
      "entities": {},
      "text": "You may be right, but the problem is that even when compared to the United States, the number of LGBTQ+ people living in relatively LGBTQ+-friendly areas here is far smaller than the number living in such areas in the U.S.\nFor example, when it comes to transgender care, only Beijing, Guangzhou, and Shanghai offer comprehensive transgender medical services. In other places, such services may not even be available, or you might have to go to different hospitals for each procedure, which is extremely inconvenient. Take Shenzhen, where I live—it’s a major city, but accessing HRT is still very difficult, so I have to go to Guangzhou."
    },
